    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21-a12">

                <pb facs="0132" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg26"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 12 in No. 183.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Grant to Mr. Janowitz</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-07-26"><hi rendition="#italic">July 26,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your letter of the 24th instant is
                    received. I do not believe that you will have any trouble when you wish to leave
                    this Monarchy; the difficulty has been to prevent the authorities from expelling
                    you before you wished to go.</p>
                <p>Yours, very truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. D. Grant</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
